{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/867500-apocalypse-tribes-as-2e-lodges","id":867500,"title":"Apocalypse Tribes as 2E Lodges","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-04-18T05:23:35-07:00","id":867500,"title":"Apocalypse Tribes as 2E Lodges","content":"As we just have <b>The Pack</b> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/get-your-motor-running/\" target=\"_blank\">spoiler with ready 2E Lodge</a> we finally can talk about project I was eager to run for whole year now \u2013 <b>How to remake <i>Apocalypse</i> Tribes into Lodges for <i>Forsaken</i> 2E games? </b>I know we have more or less write up in <i><b>Werewolf Translation Guide</b></i>, but it was for <b>WtF</b> First Edition \u2013 and from spoilers, Lodges changed greatly.<br /> <br /> Details I will later as for now do not have time, but I have first candidate I will need in my future Werewolf game I slowly build \u2013 <b>Let\u2019s talk <i>Get of Fenris</i> first as 2E Lodge!</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T05:34:51-07:00","id":867508,"title":"","content":"For ease of referance - here are is comment on Lodges design for Great <b>Acrozatarim</b>!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/867031-get-your-motor-running-the-thousand-steel-teeth-werewolf-open-development?p=867060#post867060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So yeah, the new Lodge structure revealed. Every Lodge gets a Blessing, Ban and Aspiration, as well as a Sacred Hunt and a Tools section; the latter isn't necessarily fetishes. Lodges are cults; more specifically, they are cults of the <i>hunt.</i><br /> <br /> A little something extra to note - there's an *additional* section for each Lodge of a few hundred words called Mysteries of the (insert Lodge here); these had to be cut due to space but there's an intention to release them as a web supplement. The Mysteries go into weird details about a Lodge, the heresies and blasphemies and strange occultness they engage in. So [REDACTED] believe the second tenet of the Oath of the Moon is false, while the gear dogs concern themselves with the tithe of blood that humanity owes the road spirit courts...</div> </div> </div> </div>So each Lodge is centered on particular Sacred Hunt - <b>What Prey could be <i>Get of Fenris</i>?</b> On those of not Nordic blood? It would them make almost","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T06:20:56-07:00","id":867524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/867500-apocalypse-tribes-as-2e-lodges?p=867508#post867508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So each Lodge is centered on particular Sacred Hunt - <b>What Prey could be <i>Get of Fenris</i>?</b></div> </div> </div> </div>The weak or cowardly.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T07:25:53-07:00","id":867548,"title":"","content":"That strikes me as a bit too lacking in bragging rights for the spiritual predecessor of the Blood Talons. The Get should probably hunt the biggest, nastiest stuff they can find to prove how hard they are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T07:30:44-07:00","id":867550,"title":"","content":"Then they hunt for might and bravery?<br /> <br /> While they do seem interested in the really big hunts, any prey could really fit that. You could go the Apocalypse way and have it be about corruption, but it seems like they were really disparaging of the weak or cowardly. I admit that having them as sacred prey can seem like they're only interested in targeting the weak, but that's not what sacred prey is about. Hunting the weak or cowardly is a way of culling them out so only the strong survive to hunt whatever mighty things they want to hunt. While also holding to the darker aspects of the Get.<br /> <br /> Lets not forget that a sacred prey doesn't have to be a certain kind of creature. As evidenced by the Thousand Steel Teeth, and obviously the Pure, it can be about how they go about things. The lodge hunts those who use the roads, while the Pure have wide ranging sacred prey.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-18-2016, 11:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T08:09:45-07:00","id":867568,"title":"","content":"I think maybe the weak as sacred prey would fit more with shadow lord (maybe) as getting rid of weakness seems pretty big in their philosophy. <br /> Its overly simple maybe but i'd give the Get of Fenris the sacred prey that i gave to the Blood Talons in my game. Warriors or combatants, to go with the aspect of the hunt as war or a fight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T08:36:07-07:00","id":867587,"title":"","content":"Maybe you could go back to Fenris of Norse myth were is is to eat the king of the Gods; Maybe the Get feel that they are the choosers of who gets to Rule- They hunt down people, Werewolves, spirits who are at the top of power structures. They test those in leader ship to see if they are worthy - If they kill him during the hunt all will know he is weak and unfit to rule but should he survive that he strong and has the right to rule","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/324-ardenty","name":"ardenty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar324_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T08:46:03-07:00","id":867590,"title":"","content":"What about playing up their ties to Norse mythology and making Fae creatures their sacred prey? They have historically been known to hunt Giants, Jotunn, Trolls, etc. Then their Sacred Hunt benefit could be that while on Siskur-Dah, they can recognize and pass through any door to or from the hedge that the prey has used since the Hunt was called.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T08:56:44-07:00","id":867594,"title":"","content":"Aren't the Fianna more fae-related though? Who will they hunt if the Get get fae?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T09:00:33-07:00","id":867596,"title":"","content":"I think if you wanted to go to Norse roots, you would pick the Predator Kings and Fire-Touched. They are representative of the giants, primeval beings that hearken to a more savage past, who you are always at war with but still respect for their power and ancient gifts.<br /> <br /> But then, Fenris was a descendant of these giants, and was going to bring about the end of Odin and the new ways. So perhaps it would fit better as a Predator King lodge.<br /> <br /> And, again, lets keep in mind sacred prey doesn't have to be a specific type of supernatural or mundane being. It could be bullies or leaders, those who use silver weapons or use roads, or those who disrespect something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-18-2016, 12:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T09:12:11-07:00","id":867604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/867500-apocalypse-tribes-as-2e-lodges?p=867594#post867594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aren't the Fianna more fae-related though? Who will they hunt if the Get get fae?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, nevermind then. I am not very familiar with Apocalypse, so I didn't know there was a more Fae-related Tribe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T09:16:50-07:00","id":867606,"title":"","content":"While I don't know that much about Apocalypse, what little I know suggests the Bone Gnawers might be an Iron Master Lodge, one whose members benefit from the the Hunt against the well-off; the wealthy, the politically powerful, and in general those who lack the want and hunger which so heavily defines the group's members.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T09:19:17-07:00","id":867607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/867500-apocalypse-tribes-as-2e-lodges?p=867596#post867596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think if you wanted to go to Norse roots, you would pick the Predator Kings and Fire-Touched. They are representative of the giants, primeval beings that hearken to a more savage past, who you are always at war with but still respect for their power and ancient gifts.<br /> <br /> But then, Fenris was a descendant of these giants, and was going to bring about the end of Odin and the new ways. So perhaps it would fit better as a Predator King lodge.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think Lodges have to be Tribe-exclusive any more. The sample tribe that was previewed said it was <i>mostly</i> Iron Masters, but that there were a surprising number of Bone Shadow and Storm Lord members as well. I'd imagine the Get would have Predator Kings as well as Blood Talons and probably others in its ranks.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/867500-apocalypse-tribes-as-2e-lodges?p=867596#post867596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And, again, lets keep in mind sacred prey doesn't have to be a specific type of supernatural or mundane being. It could be bullies or leaders, those who use silver weapons or use roads, or those who disrespect something.</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't have to be, but it can be. When designing Lodges, I would not want to limit myself to only using types of creature as Sacred Prey. But nor would I want to limit myself to never using them. Just depends on what's appropriate for the Lodge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T09:22:53-07:00","id":867612,"title":"","content":"Lodges are generally not tribe-limited any more. Even the tribal pillars, the lodges at the core of each tribe's philosophy, are not completely exclusive to that tribe. Non-Blood Talons can join the Lodge of Garm, for example, although few do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T09:42:31-07:00","id":867619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/867500-apocalypse-tribes-as-2e-lodges?p=867607#post867607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think Lodges have to be Tribe-exclusive any more. The sample tribe that was previewed said it was <i>mostly</i> Iron Masters, but that there were a surprising number of Bone Shadow and Storm Lord members as well. I'd imagine the Get would have Predator Kings as well as Blood Talons and probably others in its ranks.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't mean exclusively Predator Kings, but they would seem to be the core of the tribe, with primarily some Blood Talons and Storm Lords and lesser numbers of other tribes. They definitely seem more Get of Fenris the vargr that kills Odin as opposed to Fenris the Firstborn. <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Get_of_Fenris\" target=\"_blank\">In theme, at least.</a> They fit more with Dire Wolf, who was acknowledged as the mightiest of the Firstborn, even by Destroyer Wolf.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It doesn't have to be, but it can be. When designing Lodges, I would not want to limit myself to only using types of creature as Sacred Prey. But nor would I want to limit myself to never using them. Just depends on what's appropriate for the Lodge. </div> </div> </div>Oh absolutely, it's just most of the Apocalypse tribes didn't really have anything you would really put as an equivalent to sacred prey, the Garou Nation as a whole was very pro-Wyld and anti-whatever was hurting the Wyld, which doesn't really jibe with the Forsaken setting. But if you pare back the Gaia and Wyrm stuff you get a group that sounds more like the Pure, with their 'those who disrespect' something as prey, as opposed to a certain kind of being. ZealousChristian24's Bone Gnawers seemed to fit, too.<br /> <br /> I think the Silent Striders would be more of a 'type' hunter, though, focusing on the undead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-18-2016, 12:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T09:47:15-07:00","id":867621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/867500-apocalypse-tribes-as-2e-lodges?p=867606#post867606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I don't know that much about Apocalypse, what little I know suggests the Bone Gnawers might be an Iron Master Lodge, one whose members benefit from the the Hunt against the well-off; the wealthy, the politically powerful, and in general those who lack the want and hunger which so heavily defines the group's members.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd see the wealthy and powerful more as being a glass walker prey. the bone gnawer would hunt on the downtrodden. Not because they hate them, but more in the optic of a sign of respect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T11:18:47-07:00","id":867680,"title":"","content":"Just re-read <b>W20 </b>Gets write-up and here are my proposition. Take in point I want to use this in Scandinavia two timeline chronicle - one in modern night and one in Viking Era North, both stories intertwine. So I want to make this probably more Norse appropriate than rest can bother with.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:22px\"><b>Get of Fenris</b></span><br /> <i>Destroyers, </i><i>\u00dalfh\u00e9\u00f0nar</i><i>, Vargr</i><br /> <br /> Get are strongest and most loyal children of Fenris-Ur. They come from Norse culture that worshiped Fenris as most terrifying of monsters and embrace this attitude. Get want the fittest to rule - and the fittest are them, of course. When in Scandinavia old people tell to their youngsters the tales of monsters in human skin - they tell about Fenris and his Get. Mortals should remembered their place, but not be killed - kin must not forget why they feared but also admired wolves. Humanity is family, even when it needs to be pointed who is biggest dog in the pack. When Ragnarok will come, the fittest will be atop, Get will rise and eat old gods - making place for their Father.<br /> <br /> Of course, most Gets are Blood Talons, with their devotion to the Fenris-Ur and strength in battle. Surprisingly, many Gets comes also from Storm Lords - Lodges philosophy of cutting the weak reason with Lords take on not showing it in first place. In old times of Vikings, it was Get that make sure those that broke law by showing weakness, were taken out of the herd - both by Blood Talons jaws and Storm Lords claws.<br /> <br /> Even if philosophy could reason with Dire Wolf and it\u2019s Predatory Kings children, Get of Fenris is proud to turn them down. Even if Destroyers want to scare humanity and make sure that fittest will lead, it wants it also to flourish, cause other way there will be not any humanity to scare in first place. At least till the time of Ragnarok.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Totem:</b> Sk\u00f6ll</span><br /> Destroyers are following Sk\u00f6ll, son of the Fenris himself, that day till night and night till day is chasing Mani ( Moon ) and S\u00f3l ( Sun ), at least in Norse myths. In reality, Sk\u00f6ll is most persistence and loyal of Fenris children - to this way, he day and night looks for weakness in whole Uratha society, cutting weak and afraid from it\u2019s pack, to prepare for final battle in Ragnarok where gods will need to be defeated when it\u2019s father will howl for it. As one of Vargr, he assumes image of monstrous wolf that towers even over Urshuls of werewolves.<br /> <br /> Sk\u00f6ll want\u2019s his Lodge to remember people why they were afraid of wolves. To be fieriest, loyal and dedicated. Ready for each howl of Fenris. And to show that Children of Fenris are true power to be reckoned with.<br /> <br /> Lodges sacred duty and mixing of Tribes under Sk\u00f6ll probably lead to popular claim that he was symbol of Storm Lords in Forsaken society in times of Vikings.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Bonds</b></span><br /> <b>Blessing: </b>When she spends Willpower to add dice to a Brawl or Weaponry roll to attack, or an Athletics roll to dodge, the Lodge member gains the rote quality on that roll.<br /> <br /> <b>Aspiration:</b> To curl any weakness in adherent pack. ( Think also about \u201cscare mortals\u201d here, not sure with what to go )<br /> <br /> <b>Ban:</b> A Lodge member cannot let anyone to call into question his power.<br /> <br /> <b>The Sacred Hunt</b><br /> The Lodge Sacred Hunt grants your character the ability to track prey that shown signs of weakness to other being in last lunar month. While the prey is in his eyesight, your character can upgrade any bashing damage to lethal damage that is inflicted to prey in marking her shown as weak - or to grant Condition marking prey\u2019s lower status.<br /> <br /> This ability lead to Lodges hunting on outlaws from calling Ergi in Viking society (see <b>Dark Eras</b> chapter <i>The Wolf and The Raven</i> ). In modern times, most Lodge members know that culture changed and weakness comes from other stands than sexuality or gender roles. Still, there are some old and hardened in cult that do not see this differences. In both eras, this \u201clooking for weakness\u201d made Get\u2019s reputation of often shattering alliance with rest of Tribes of Moon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 04-18-2016, 04:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T11:34:09-07:00","id":867693,"title":"","content":"Alright, that sounds pretty cool. Who's next?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T13:01:52-07:00","id":867757,"title":"","content":"Here are the Sacred Prey I'd see for the different Tribes:<br /> <br /> Black Furies - Those who have harmed women<br /> Bone Gnawers - Those that would mistreat the downtrodden.<br /> Children of Gaia - Warmongers and others who disrupt peace.<br /> Fianna - The fae.<br /> Get of Fenris - My initial thought was worthy foes, but I like what was written above.<br /> Glass Walkers - Those who hide behind wealth and power.<br /> Red Talons - Those who disrespect Nature.<br /> Shadow Lords - Traitors, especially their own.<br /> Silent Striders - Those who escape into other realms.<br /> Silver Fangs - Alphas and others in leadership roles.<br /> Uktena - Corrupted souls and spirits.<br /> Wendigo - Those who disrespect indigenous cultures.<br /> Stargazers - Purveyors of hatred and ignorance.<br /> Black Spiral Dancers - The innocent and virtuous.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T13:22:27-07:00","id":867771,"title":"","content":"I'm guessing the Black Spiral Dancers would work best as a predominantly Bale Hound lodge. We also need to figure out why they'd be called the Black Spiral Dancers in a setting that lacks a Black Spiral in which to Dance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T13:45:07-07:00","id":867796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/867500-apocalypse-tribes-as-2e-lodges?p=867771#post867771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm guessing the Black Spiral Dancers would work best as a predominantly Bale Hound lodge. We also need to figure out why they'd be called the Black Spiral Dancers in a setting that lacks a Black Spiral in which to Dance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cause they draging humanity in &quot;<a href=\"https://www.google.pl/search?q=Black+hole&amp;biw=1366&amp;bih=643&amp;source=lnms&amp;tbm=isch&amp;sa=X&amp;ved=0ahUKEwi4uIeQhJnMAhVMhiwKHV_HDrUQ_AUIBigB\" target=\"_blank\">Black Spiral</a>&quot;? <i>Dancer</i> points to their manipulative ways - <b>Forsaken</b> version would be much more scheming - leading that end goal of humanity is Black Spiral - what modern physists call Black Hole - and is end of life. In reality, it's end goal of all Bale Hounds, at least in 1E.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blasphemies</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Eventually, so the Bale Hounds believe, the world itself will be Wounded.<br /> (...)<br /> The perceived truth behind the actions of the Asah Gadar is simple enough, yet rarely understood by outsiders: <b>the world is fundamentally and naturally inclined toward negativity and darkness.</b><br /> (...)<br /> Wounds spread through the Shadow, crime rates rise, wars become worse and use more devastating weapons. <b>An inexorable spiral into negativity is a difficult argument to refute.</b><br /> <br /> The Bale Hounds believe this descent cannot be successfully opposed. Rather than fight to the death trying to prevent the inevitable, the Asah Gadar werewolves attempt to usher in the new era so that they are on the winning side. By fearing the end of everything, they fall into their new roles. By seeking to survive and stand by the victors, they willingly defect.</div> </div> </div> </div>Black Spirals Dancers are those of Bale Hounds that want to spin humanity more and more in the end of universe all Asah Gadar believe will come to humans. They seed entropy, disappear and - for most - hunt &quot;Beams of Light&quot; in civilization - to douse any unneeded points of this resistance. End is Black Spiral. Let's &quot;dance&quot; with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T14:12:01-07:00","id":867810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/867500-apocalypse-tribes-as-2e-lodges?p=867796#post867796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Cause they draging humanity in &quot;<a href=\"https://www.google.pl/search?q=Black+hole&amp;biw=1366&amp;bih=643&amp;source=lnms&amp;tbm=isch&amp;sa=X&amp;ved=0ahUKEwi4uIeQhJnMAhVMhiwKHV_HDrUQ_AUIBigB\" target=\"_blank\">Black Spiral</a>&quot;? <i>Dancer</i> points to their manipulative ways - <b>Forsaken</b> version would be much more scheming - leading that end goal of humanity is Black Spiral - what modern physists call Black Hole - and is end of life. In reality, it's end goal of all Bale Hounds, at least in 1E.</div> </div> </div> </div>Incorrect. Bale Hounds, and their Maeljin masters wish to drag the world into a senseless hellish existence to better feed their dark appetites. There's no essence to be gotten from the end of all things.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/867500-apocalypse-tribes-as-2e-lodges?p=867796#post867796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Black Spirals Dancers are those of Bale Hounds that want to spin humanity more and more in the end of universe all Asah Gadar believe will come to humans. They seed entropy, disappear and - for most - hunt &quot;Beams of Light&quot; in civilization - to douse any unneeded points of this resistance. End is Black Spiral. Let's &quot;dance&quot; with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a difference between planned obsolescence and the inarticulation of society at large with seeking its wholesome destruction.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T14:21:03-07:00","id":867814,"title":"","content":"To be fair the Bale Hounds of Sloth want nothing going on, but they still want there to be someplace for nothing to be happening. Or not happening.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T14:28:57-07:00","id":867821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/867500-apocalypse-tribes-as-2e-lodges?p=867771#post867771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm guessing the Black Spiral Dancers would work best as a predominantly Bale Hound lodge. We also need to figure out why they'd be called the Black Spiral Dancers in a setting that lacks a Black Spiral in which to Dance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe there is a Black Spiral? Heck, maybe it's the Lodge Totem, a twisted lesser Maeljin that drags people deeper and deeper into the darkest parts of themselves, and the Lodge seeks to feed their patron through both corrupting people and by physically taking humans and Uratha to the foul Wounds where their lord physically manifests?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T17:32:39-07:00","id":867940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/867500-apocalypse-tribes-as-2e-lodges?p=867814#post867814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair the Bale Hounds of Sloth want nothing going on, but they still want there to be someplace for nothing to be happening. Or not happening.</div> </div> </div> </div>Savage apathy isn't the same as mere laziness.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#231F20\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\">Sloth is not mere laziness. There is nothing to fear about laziness and very little negative spiritual resonance born of such an attitude. When a werewolf is sworn to the Maeljin of Sloth, his disregard for others takes on a savage and cold-hearted clarity. True sloth is the utter lack of care for anyone or anything. No friends deserve to be defended, no lovers deserve to be cared for and no packmate is worth shedding blood for. Everything and everyone is <span style=\"font-family:Goudy-Italic\"><i>below </i><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\">the Bale Hounds of Beliar. In fact, many even care little for their own lives, especially those fanatical enough to conceive of their own godhood once the Maeljin rise to dominance. </span></span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T17:46:48-07:00","id":867955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/867500-apocalypse-tribes-as-2e-lodges?p=867680#post867680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Bonds</b></span><br /> <b>Blessing: </b>When she spends Willpower to add dice to a Brawl or Weaponry roll to attack, or an Athletics roll to dodge, the Lodge member gains the rote quality on that roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThat is considerably higher-end than I would suggest for a combat-boost blessing. You need to be wary of any mechanic granting rote on an attack pool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T17:49:03-07:00","id":867958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/867500-apocalypse-tribes-as-2e-lodges?p=867940#post867940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Savage apathy isn't the same as mere laziness.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, but I was referring to this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The true appeal of Beliar\u2019s path is the theory that Beliar will eventually triumph over all Maeljin. Eventually, the other Maeljin will run out of things to covet or despise; even they will inevitably run out of energy. As the universe tilts on toward ultimate entropy, Beliar gains more strength. At the end of it all, when none of the stars are left to bother with light, the lord of Sloth will be the entirety of creation. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T19:54:27-07:00","id":868084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/867500-apocalypse-tribes-as-2e-lodges?p=867955#post867955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bThat is considerably higher-end than I would suggest for a combat-boost blessing. You need to be wary of any mechanic granting rote on an attack pool.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's first draft for any Lodge I write for here - I will revisit them after <b>The Pack</b> will come to balance them nicely. More important question is this - <b>Do my <i>Get of Fenris</i> are &quot;Get-enough&quot; and works as Forsaken Lodge? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T19:55:02-07:00","id":868085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/867500-apocalypse-tribes-as-2e-lodges?p=867757#post867757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Silver Fangs - Alphas and others in leadership roles.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe leaders that went crazy with power? Dictators and political figures that won't release their grip on power, maybe even like when Wolf grew weak. Maybe Wolf wasn't physically weak, but mentally? Could Black Spirals have found Wolf's remains in the depths of the labirinth of the first Wound, and plan on reuniting the corpse with its heart to bring forth the ultimate hunter, allowing it to devour this corrupted reality?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5446-binaly","name":"BinAly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5446_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"146"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-19T02:04:50-07:00","id":868279,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/867500-apocalypse-tribes-as-2e-lodges?p=867955#post867955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bThat is considerably higher-end than I would suggest for a combat-boost blessing. You need to be wary of any mechanic granting rote on an attack pool.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> What about a +1L weapon rating to any attack they make (or +1A for attacks that do aggravated damage)? Like, if they fire a gun, stab with a knife, use gauru claws or bite, punch in hishu, it gets a +1L to the weapon rating, or in the case of hishu attacks it turns their brawl attacks into 1L or 0L. It's what I've agreed with my storyteller for a modified Lodge of Garm in 2e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-19T03:47:35-07:00","id":868305,"title":"","content":"I have maybe a crazy idea - <b>What if Black Spiral Dancers worship every Malejin on equal, changing their now patron in &quot;Dance&quot;, working with changed Vices? </b>Basically, they can have any Malejin Vice if they &quot;Dance&quot; for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-19T04:11:51-07:00","id":868310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/867500-apocalypse-tribes-as-2e-lodges?p=868084#post868084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's first draft for any Lodge I write for here - I will revisit them after <b>The Pack</b> will come to balance them nicely. More important question is this - <b>Do my <i>Get of Fenris</i> are &quot;Get-enough&quot; and works as Forsaken Lodge? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></b></div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know enough about the Get of Fenris to say whether they're Get enough, to be honest.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fumus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/867500-apocalypse-tribes-as-2e-lodges?p=868279#post868279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What about a +1L weapon rating to any attack they make (or +1A for attacks that do aggravated damage)? Like, if they fire a gun, stab with a knife, use gauru claws or bite, punch in hishu, it gets a +1L to the weapon rating, or in the case of hishu attacks it turns their brawl attacks into 1L or 0L. It's what I've agreed with my storyteller for a modified Lodge of Garm in 2e.</div> </div> </div> </div> \u200bWell the Lodge of Garm are one of the sample Lodges in The Pack so you'll get to see what their blessing and sacred prey are soon enough!<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-19T04:54:43-07:00","id":868322,"title":"","content":"They are? That's awesome, I didn't realise. Now I'm looking forward to the pack even more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-19T06:31:28-07:00","id":868371,"title":"","content":"Yep. The Garmir are the example tribal pillar Lodge in the book. It was a toss-up between them and the Lodge of Death but, since I wanted to put the Eaters of the Dead in, the Lodge of Death would have meant two lodges with relatively close (though by no means identical) sacred prey specialisations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-19T07:06:29-07:00","id":868394,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/867500-apocalypse-tribes-as-2e-lodges?p=868371#post868371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yep. The Garmir are the example tribal pillar Lodge in the book. It was a toss-up between them and the Lodge of Death but, since I wanted to put the Eaters of the Dead in, the Lodge of Death would have meant two lodges with relatively close (though by no means identical) sacred prey specialisations.</div> </div> </div> </div>I must say, the tribal pillars are a fantastic concept though I think I'm a little biased when my favorite tribe is the one getting the first tribal pillar written up.<br /> <br /> I really like the Eaters of the Dead from their write-up in the core, that said the Temple of Apollo is the one I look forward to most after the Garmir, if it's what it sounds like (a lodge of helios worshippers) then I am going to do so much with it. And then once we get a better look at example blessings I'm going to give the Einherjar an attempt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-19T07:14:09-07:00","id":868397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/867500-apocalypse-tribes-as-2e-lodges?p=867524#post867524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The weak or cowardly.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's how the Pure operate (choosing prey for their perceived flaws). Forsaken aligned to prey they perceive as most worthy/greatest threat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-19T07:49:56-07:00","id":868424,"title":"","content":"I like the Smoke Drinker. The idea of giving him pit stops and waystations on his eternal run from That Which Is Broken has some nice stories built into it and definitely shakes the standard tribal setup while also bringing in some ideas from Blasphemies, namely the cults.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/867500-apocalypse-tribes-as-2e-lodges?p=868397#post868397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's how the Pure operate (choosing prey for their perceived flaws). Forsaken aligned to prey they perceive as most worthy/greatest threat.</div> </div> </div> </div>These are lodges, not tribes confined to either of the sects, and it seemed to me the Get of Fenris fit the Pure better than Forsaken anyways. Specifically as a camp of the Predator Kings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-19T09:12:02-07:00","id":868476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/867500-apocalypse-tribes-as-2e-lodges?p=868397#post868397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's how the Pure operate (choosing prey for their perceived flaws). Forsaken aligned to prey they perceive as most worthy/greatest threat.</div> </div> </div> </div>The THOUSAND STEEL TEETH <i>do not</i> have particular Sacred Prey, yet they get benefit after ritual itself. I start to think we wrongly assumed that Lodges get you second Sacred Prey - they <b>get</b> you <i>only</i> second Siskur Dah benefit. Your Tribe still dictates your main Sacred Prey. If that's the case - easily my version of <i>Get of Fenris</i> will have still mostly Uratha ( from Blood Talons ) and Urged ( from Storm Lords ) - both sounds fitting for modern Gets.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>2E Lodges spoiler</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Sacred Hunt<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The Lodge Sacred Hunt grants your character the ability to track prey even while she is in a moving vehicle; she suffers no penalties to the tracking attempt for the prey using a vehicle. While the prey is in a vehicle, your character can downgrade any lethal damage to bashing damage that is inflicted due to being hit by a vehicle, falling off a moving vehicle or her own vehicle being damaged or destroyed.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/867500-apocalypse-tribes-as-2e-lodges?p=868397#post868397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">These are lodges, not tribes confined to either of the sects, and it seemed to me the Get of Fenris fit the Pure better than Forsaken anyways. Specifically as a camp of the Predator Kings.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm still much more see them as mainly Blood Talons Lodge ( not only because of Fenris ), but I would like to see your take on them as Predator Kings. I do not agree with that assesment, but would like how you would make them Pure as Lodge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 04-19-2016, 12:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-19T09:22:27-07:00","id":868487,"title":"","content":"From the admittedly somewhat unreliable sample size of one it does appear that a lodge prescribes a <i>method </i>of hunting rather than a <i>target. </i>Not a who but a how.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-19T09:25:33-07:00","id":868489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/867500-apocalypse-tribes-as-2e-lodges?p=868476#post868476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The THOUSAND STEEL TEETH <i>do not</i> have particular Sacred Prey, yet they get benefit after ritual itself. I start to think we wrongly assumed that Lodges get you second Sacred Prey - they <b>get</b> you <i>only</i> second Siskur Dah benefit.</div> </div> </div> </div>It looks more like a refinement of how they hunt, at least with this lodge.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Thousand Steel Teeth choose those who would take to the road as their sacred prey, hunting humans and Claimed and Uratha alike upon steel steeds. Holiness is in the snarl of the machine and the thunder of the wind, and divine exhilaration in the sheer speed and adrenaline and impact of vehicle against flesh. So many prey think they can outrun the judgment of the hunt or the wrath of the Urdaga. So many prey think that taming a beast of metal makes them a superior predator than the wolves. The Thousand Steel Teeth prove them all wrong. </div> </div> </div>Sacred prey is not a special mechanic, however, it's just a focus of the tribe or lodge. The Eaters of the Dead may focus on vampires, based on their entry in the core book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-19-2016, 12:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-19T09:53:42-07:00","id":868511,"title":"","content":"Lodges possess refinements of the sacred hunt. In some cases this is a specific type of prey; in other cases, it is something else to do with the hunt, such as an element of the context or the pursuit or the kill.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-19T10:12:36-07:00","id":868529,"title":"","content":"Get of Fenris, when not completely subsumed into the Blood Talons, sound like a particular Nazi organization within the tribe, from my point of view.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-19T10:22:44-07:00","id":868541,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/867500-apocalypse-tribes-as-2e-lodges?p=868529#post868529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Get of Fenris, when not completely subsumed into the Blood Talons, sound like a particular Nazi organization within the tribe, from my point of view.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think some of them did walk down that road, too. But I was thinking more because of their survivalist bent, though that's a good point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-19T10:26:35-07:00","id":868544,"title":"","content":"So a Predator King / Ivory Claw lodge then?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-19T10:32:21-07:00","id":868549,"title":"","content":"The Ivory Claws seem more about familial lines, so while I'm sure many were on that side during the rise of the Nazi regime, it seems just as likely others were on the other side of things. Presumably one faction would have been targeted after the war by whoever felt most affronted by their acts. Mortal Nazi hunters still exist, I'm sure werewolves would still be out there in some way.<br /> <br /> I just think it would fit for, primarily, both Predator Kings and Blood Talons. Other tribes could join if they were about war, even those seen less warlike, as I'm sure there's Bone Shadows and Fire-Touched who have been built for battle among spirits and are veterans of particularly crazed wars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-19T11:59:21-07:00","id":868631,"title":"","content":"Shadow Lords (Lodge of the Storm Lords). They hunt down traitors who left to join the Pure tribes/Bale Hounds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1250-shadowlost","name":"Shadowlost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1250_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"155"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-19T20:48:29-07:00","id":869071,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/867500-apocalypse-tribes-as-2e-lodges?p=868549#post868549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just think it would fit for, primarily, both Predator Kings and Blood Talons. Other tribes could join if they were about war, even those seen less warlike, as I'm sure there's Bone Shadows and Fire-Touched who have been built for battle among spirits and are veterans of particularly crazed wars.</div> </div> </div> </div>I could see this, but there is one, simple question - <b>HOW Pure uratha can follow Fenris ( or his child ) totem? </b>Especially, with Dire Wolf / Fenris animosity. When you joins side of one, you are enemy of another.<br /> <br /> Also, still waiting for counter write-up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-19T21:21:53-07:00","id":869091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/867500-apocalypse-tribes-as-2e-lodges?p=869071#post869071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could see this, but there is one, simple question - <b>HOW Pure uratha can follow Fenris ( or his child ) totem? </b>Especially, with Dire Wolf / Fenris animosity. When you joins side of one, you are enemy of another.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Firstborn didn't exist in Apocalypse. They are not the Get of Fenris-Ur, they are the Get of Fenris from Norse myth. They follow a twisted Shadow version of the vargr, not the Firstborn.<br /> <br /> It's just a name.<br /> <br /> I wasn't interested in writing something up, but you asked how to do it. I think if you were going to stay faithful to the settings, everyone wouldn't fit neatly on the sides of the Forsaken.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-20T00:46:23-07:00","id":869161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/867500-apocalypse-tribes-as-2e-lodges?p=869091#post869091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Firstborn didn't exist in Apocalypse. They are not the Get of Fenris-Ur, they are the Get of Fenris from Norse myth. They follow a twisted Shadow version of the vargr, not the Firstborn.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Dark Eras</b> <i>The Wolf and The Raven </i>states that, indeed, Fenris-Ur <i>is</i> Fenris of Norse myths. Not sticking to Fenris-Ur is denial of a <b>WtF</b> setting. We try to recreate <b>Apocalypse</b> Tribes in <b>Forsaken</b> setting, not running <b>Apocalypse</b> with <b>Forsaken</b> rules.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/867500-apocalypse-tribes-as-2e-lodges?p=869091#post869091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's just a name.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it's not. If that would be just name <i>Black Furres</i> could be called Feminists, <i>Fianna</i> be Fae Lovers, <i>Black Spirals Dancers</i> would simply be all Bale Hounds and alike. The whole charm of recreating <b>Apocalypse</b> Tribes as Lodges is trying to take their cultural heritage as part of Lodges philosophy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/867500-apocalypse-tribes-as-2e-lodges?p=869091#post869091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wasn't interested in writing something up, but you asked how to do it. I think if you were going to stay faithful to the settings, everyone wouldn't fit neatly on the sides of the Forsaken.</div> </div> </div> </div>With that I agree - for example for <i>Silver Fangs</i> I would go with Lodge splintered in to two mirror groups in Storm Lords and Ivory Claws ( probably connected to House of Sun and Moon ), both working for Falcon Totem on more or less the same terms. Many other <b>Apocalypse </b>groups could work like this.<br /> <br /> Only <i>Get of Fenris</i>, from <b>Forsaken</b> game design reasons, should not be splintered into Forsaken and Pure groups. On the other hand, I'm inclined in to remaking <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><i>Eiwaz Mot</i> Lodge ( from <b>Blasphemies</b> ) for the Pure Lodge, probably splinter from the <i>Get</i>'s originals, working for Dire Wolf - it always was striking to be as more Pure creation, with whole supremacist take.</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-20T08:41:10-07:00","id":869342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/867500-apocalypse-tribes-as-2e-lodges?p=869161#post869161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Dark Eras</b> <i>The Wolf and The Raven </i>states that, indeed, Fenris-Ur <i>is</i> Fenris of Norse myths. Not sticking to Fenris-Ur is denial of a <b>WtF</b> setting. We try to recreate <b>Apocalypse</b> Tribes in <b>Forsaken</b> setting, not running <b>Apocalypse</b> with <b>Forsaken</b> rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>More specifically it says they <i>believe </i>their own myths have permeated Norse culture, which is why the vargr is called Fenris. Just like the Ragnarok didn't happen, there's no cause to believe the rest of it was accurate.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">No, it's not. If that would be just name </span></span></span><i>Black Furres</i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> could be called Feminists, </span></span></span><i>Fianna</i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> be Fae Lovers, </span></span></span><i>Black Spirals Dancers</i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> would simply be all Bale Hounds and alike.</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> It's more that because Fenris is not actual Fenris, the Black Furies are not African Berserkers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">The whole charm of recreating </span></span></span><b>Apocalypse</b><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> Tribes as Lodges is trying to take their cultural heritage as part of Lodges philosophy.</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> You left out the fascism and racial bias, their hatred of dishonor, their blasphemous belief that they are the children of Fenris, the fierce protection of their Wolf-blooded, who are also descendants of Fenris, their chasing Odin to begin the Ragnarok. To the point that your version of the Get of Fenris has only really the name in common.<br /> <br /> Incidentally having read the tribe book I would agree with others that hunting the dishonorable would fit as a sacred prey variant.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-20T09:49:42-07:00","id":869390,"title":"","content":"If Get of Fenris = Blood Talons, why would you make a lodge?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-20T11:28:38-07:00","id":869462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/867500-apocalypse-tribes-as-2e-lodges?p=869390#post869390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If Get of Fenris = Blood Talons, why would you make a lodge?</div> </div> </div> </div>I <b>did not</b> written that <i>Get </i>= Blood Talons. In my write up I even mentioned that other large part of the Lodge are Storm Lords - in pointing even what was their mission in it.<br /> <br /> In this topic I pointed that <i>Get of Fenris</i> <b>cannot </b>be Pure Lodge not because they philosophy clash ( they could possibly work with most of Pure ) - but because their Totem ( Fenris-Ur and his child, Sk\u00f6ll ) are affiliated with Forsaken Tribes, not Pure. You <b>cannot</b> make a Lodge that will work under Totem that is direct enemy to your Tribe from seven millenia now. ( I mean here about Fenris-Ur and Pure Tribes conflict ).<br /> <br /> You <b>can</b> have very similar Lodge on enemies side, with different Totem. But this Lodge will not be called <i>Get of Fenris</i>, as Fenris-Ur in <b>WtF</b> is affiliated with and supporting Forsaken Tribes. For Pure side, I would more than enough support rewritting <i>Eiwaz Mot</i> for this purpose. ( They sound as <b>WtA</b> Get\u2019s Pure-like knock-off in first place ).<br /> <br /> In slowly prepared by me <i>Silver Fangs</i> Lodge example - their Totem is Falcon, so he is not directly tied to any Firstborn - and as such, he <b>can</b> support both Forsaken and Pure as his \u201cchildren\u201d. So <i>Silver Fangs</i> Lodge will have Storm Lords and Ivory Claws factions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/867500-apocalypse-tribes-as-2e-lodges?p=869342#post869342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> More specifically it says they <i>believe </i>their own myths have permeated Norse culture, which is why the vargr is called Fenris. Just like the Ragnarok didn't happen, there's no cause to believe the rest of it was accurate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Direct quote about matter from <b>Dark Eras </b>chapter with bolds by me...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>\u201dThe Wolf and The Raven\u201d</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Regardless of the truth of the gods, the Uratha know their own history has permeated Scandinavian mythology.</b> This is not that unusual; every human religion seems to touch on some form of truth. <b>But while the details may not be entirely correct, for some the parallels are too great to ignore, particularly the monstrous wolves known as the vargr. Fenris-Ur, the Destroyer, is destined to bring about Ragnar\u00f6k by consuming Odin. </b>He is bound by a mighty chain, interpreted as a ban, preventing him from doing so. Mani and his sister S\u00f3l are pursued through the skies by the vargr Hati and Sk\u00f6ll respectively, to be consumed during the same period.</div> </div> </div> </div>And later...<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>\u201dThe Wolf and The Raven\u201d</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">While human storytellers have clearly taken liberties<b>, few</b> <b>Uratha doubt the tale relates to Fenris-Ur. </b>Of course the bindings in the tale are not physical, but a ban, though the Firstborn\u2019s role in the doom of the gods confuses some members of the tribe.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>\u201dThe Wolf and The Raven\u201d</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Despite his role in binding their tribal totem, the Blood Talons hold a deep respect for the god of justice and war, T\u00fdr. His unflinching sacrifice of his hand to the <b>jaws of Fenris-Ur</b> captures the essence of the tribe\u2019s Oath.</div> </div> </div> </div>If <i>Get of Fenris </i>is Lodge with roots in Norse Scandinavia, and most of Uratha believed to Fenris = Fenris-Ur, so <i>Get of Fenris</i> is directly working for the Fenris-Ur, simple. Especially, as in <b>WtF</b>, some Uratha <b>can </b>talk with Fenris-Ur or any other Firstborn to and ask them if Fenris = Fenris-Ur. Like you do not undermine that Mani is Father Moon, you do not make this with Firstborns names, specially this direct. It\u2019s simply game\u2019s fact.<br /> <br /> You can have your opinion, but for me questioning this is illogical - if you do not like my assumption ( or rather following game as written ) you can make yours version of <i>Get</i>, coming from Fenris =/= Fenris-Ur. But personally I do not really see the point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/867500-apocalypse-tribes-as-2e-lodges?p=869342#post869342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> You left out the fascism and racial bias, their hatred of dishonor, their blasphemous belief that they are the children of Fenris, the fierce protection of their Wolf-blooded, who are also descendants of Fenris, their chasing Odin to begin the Ragnarok. To the point that your version of the Get of Fenris has only really the name in common..</div> </div> </div> </div>I did not dwell in details for now, yes, making basic proposition on Lodge. I will extend on those stuff in second version. Information I was writing based on <b>W20</b> write-up of Tribe and it was much more sounding as looking over \u201cweakness\u201d than \u201cdishonor\u201d - still, in ancient Norse culture \u201cweakness\u201d ( called Ergi ) was as much as being coward, dishonor, \u2018being like women\u2019 ( passive homosexuality ) and few other meanings.<br /> <br /> Fascism and racial bias could be marked in \u201cold and hardened\u201d part of write-up, even if I do not sure if Norse really were this on \u201cracial purity\u201d that Nazis seemed to imply.<br /> <br /> Lodge Totem - Sk\u00f6ll - is, literally, chasing after Sun and Moon in their believes. But yes, you are right - Ragnarok side should be deepen. I will probably point there that Lodge feel partially obsolete, as they pointed next big man conflicts ( like World Wars ) as next Ragnarok times that still did not come.<br /> <br /> And - What is this all &quot;blasphemous&quot; belief they are children of Fenris?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 04-20-2016, 02:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-20T11:52:41-07:00","id":869493,"title":"","content":"Even in Basra, with Fenris potentially stalking around, no one has actually seen the Firstborn and survived to tell the tale. Red Wolf is probably the only one that would hold an AMA with its tribeswolves.<br /> <br /> What you're seeing is the Uratha believing Norse myth has taken something from Uratha mythology and merged it with their own beliefs, with the chain representing a ban and not actually being a chain that Odin forged, because Odin represents, but at this time there were Uratha and Blood Talons who had never heard of the Norse or their myths. The Get of Fenris believe Norse myth is absolutely right, as they are children of Fenris and the Vanir Sigurd and hunt for Odin due to his dishonorable and cowardly nature and the fact that he literally bound Fenris in chains. And to be fair to them, it might be entirely true.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A<span style=\"font-family:inherit\">nd - What is this all &quot;blasphemous&quot; belief they are children of Fenris?</span> </div> </div> </div> As I stated above, the Get are the direct descendants of Fenris. They do not join his tribe like the Blood Talons. It places more of an emphasis on the spirit of Fenris than Urfarah, which fits for a lodge.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-20-2016, 02:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-21T11:16:29-07:00","id":870370,"title":"","content":"Presenting my take on Bone Gnawers as urban information wolves. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Bone Gnawers</b></span><br /> <i>Children of Rat, </i><i>Scavengers</i><i>, Punks</i><br /> <br /> \u201cWhatever works.\u201d It\u2019s motto for the wolf Children of Rat. One of oldest ( some say THE oldest ) of Lodges is about survival. But survival in world after Sundering, where Hunters Paradise is no more. Many say that future Bone Gnawers foreseen rise of humanity and prepared for years to come before final blow on Urfarah put the end to Pangea. Others say that Mother Rat was best informed as she get all about Wolf\u2019s weakness from Plague King, as his consort, even when she betrayed him later. But it\u2019s all myths and legends now. And <i>now</i> is what Bone Gnawers are all about.<br /> <br /> Scavengers were always with humans, on the low and outskirts, with wretched and downrotten. Eating scraps from Man\u2019s table, convincing to be only common dogs, they have best place to listen what humans say when no one sees. Bone Gnawers are always where humanity pretends it does not have problems with it\u2019s own society. And it\u2019s always have.<br /> <br /> Even if commonly disdain for their society circles and Totem, Punks are known as best information gatherers in area with human populations - the larger, the better. Like the rats under auspice of their Mother, they feel best in crowd. They are also then less seen, with their somehow odd and disturbing to rest of Uratha quirks.<br /> <br /> Even if Lodge is open to all Tribes members, not many outside of Iron Masters join them. Children of Red Wolf makes perfect Children of Rat, as both groups motto\u2019s are almost the same. Few really devoted urban shamans from Bone Shadows join it, reconciling \u201cbone\u201d parts of groups names in looking over deaths and dead in cities. Very dedicated Hunters in Darkness, fighting Beshilu, enter Lodge to understand their enemy better. Surprisingly, many Ghost Wolves become Bone Gnawers, understanding living outside of main society. But it\u2019s okay - Rat will take each that accept her.<br /> <br /> <b>Totem:</b> Rat<br /> Mother Rat is patron of Gnawers. She is spirit of filth, crowds and doing what\u2019s necessary - but also knowledge and information. Most Uratha despise her as taking her for Plague King of Beshilu Host. Truth is those two entities where couple eons ago, preparing rats to take the world. But when Urfarah hunt the Plague King and his kind, she give up King for the lives of her children. And Wolf let them live, as he was hunting King for breaking his rules in Pangea. From then on, Rat do everything whats need to be done to survive. However, Plague King never forgave her and still is hunting her and spiritual kin. This means that Beshilu actively tries to kill any Rat spirits they can find in nearby. Kill - or maybe do something much worse...<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Bonds</b></span><br /> <b>Blessing: </b>The Lodge member starts with Perfect Impression on every Social Maneuvering from Urban Choir spirits and people in lower strata of society. When spending Willpower to add dices on Survival roll, he gains the rote quality on that roll.<br /> <b>Aspiration:</b> To gather information on local population.<br /> <b>Ban:</b> A Lodge member cannot let downrotten to suffer.<br /> <b>The Sacred Hunt</b><br /> The Lodge Sacred Hunt grants your character the ability to track prey even while she is in ugliest part of town; she suffers no penalties to the tracking attempt for sight or smell in urban centers.<br /> <br /> Many of Bone Gnawers Lodge members have those Conditions.<br /> <br /> <b>Homeless (Persistent)</b><br /> Character does not have his own home and probably live on the street. She cannot also found new one. If character do not sleep in some kind of shelter, she does not get Willpower from resting for that night. Forced starvation or dehydration can lead her to Deprived Condition or even Sick Tilt. Long time without shower makes other people to be off putted by her presence - every Social Maneuvering with character without this Condition starts on one level lower Impression than normal. Character also cannot buy dots in Resources Merit.<br /> <b>Possible Sources:</b> Life tragedy, like fire in previous house or loss of family. Lost of wealth or job.<br /> <b>Resolution:</b> Getting steady income enough to sustain living in normal accommodation for at least month. Help from close ones, letting to support character.<br /> <b>Beat:</b> Character makes other people to leave his presence. Character get\u2019s free food, clothes or money on them from other.<br /> <br /> <b>Outsider</b> <b>(Persistent)</b><br /> This character looks and acts counter to the main society. Depending on location or history era, this character can be from untouchable caste Dalit in India or Burakumin in Japan, gay, hippie, punk, goth or any radical counterculture of the time. Character have -1 to -3 penalty on social rolls with others depending on target conservative worldview. Mainstream target would have -1 and ultraconservative would have -3 penalty. Character also add one more Door for each penalty point to the target\u2019s pool.<br /> <b>Possible Sources:</b> Skin color or sexuality. Loss of status in society. Teenage rebellion.<br /> <b>Beat:</b> Whenever characters status leads to conflict with authorities or community.<br /> <b>Resolution: </b>Character integrates with mainstream. She changes her act and look to be with norm or even is lifted to proper society of location and era.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 04-21-2016, 02:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-21T11:59:45-07:00","id":870423,"title":"","content":"I like the idea of the Silver Fangs being Ivory Claw defectors to the forsaken.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Freelance Writer: WtF Night Horrors: Shunned by the Moon<br /> United States Sailor, First Responder,Ally, Bad Speller, Book Hoarder and all around Nerd.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2640-rx781a","name":"rx781a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2640_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-21T14:01:57-07:00","id":870597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/867500-apocalypse-tribes-as-2e-lodges?p=870370#post870370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Presenting my take on Bone Gnawers as urban information wolves. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Bone Gnawers</b></span><br /> <i>Children of Rat, </i><i>Scavengers</i><i>, Punks</i><br /> <br /> \u201cWhatever works.\u201d Its the motto for the Uratha children of Rat. One of oldest (some say the oldest) of Lodges it's creed is concerned about survival. Many say that future Bone Gnawers foresaw the rise of humanity and prepared for years to come before final the blow on Urfarah that put an end to Pangaea. Others say that Mother Rat knew about the Wolf\u2019s weakness her consort, the Plague King even when she betrayed him later. The truth lies somewhere amid myth now.<br /> <br /> The Scavengers were always among humanity, on the low and outskirts, with the wretched and downthrodden. Eating scraps from Man\u2019s table, behaving common dogs, until it came the time to hunt.<br /> <br /> Even if commonly disdained because of their socioeconomic status and their Totem, the Scavengers are known as best information gatherers within urban territories - the larger, the better. Like the rats under auspice of their Matriarch, they feel best in crowds, hiding in plain sight.<br /> <br /> Even with the Lodge open to all Tribes, not many outside of Iron Masters join them. Children of Red Wolf make the perfect Children for Rat, as both groups' motto are almost the same. Few devoted urban shamans from Bone Shadows join it, becoming veritable urban encyclopedias. Intriguingly some dedicated Hunters in Darkness enter Lodge to better understand their enemy. Surprisingly, many Ghost Wolves become Bone Gnawers, understanding living outside of the mainstream. But it\u2019s alright - Rat accepts all her children equally.<br /> <br /> <b>Totem:</b> Rat<br /> The patron of the Gnawers is Rat. A spirit of filth, crowds and doing what\u2019s necessary - but also knowledge and information. Most Uratha despise her as believing her to be part of the hateful Plague King. The truth is that She was the matriarch to the progenitor of Beshilu, preparing rats to take the world. But when Urfarah hunted the Plague King and it's kind, she give it up for the lives of her children. And Wolf let them live in return. From then on, Rat do everything whats need to be done to survive. However, the Plague King never forgave her, cursing her with it's dying screech. The Bone Gnawers find Beshilu among it's greatest foes.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Bonds</b></span><br /> <b>Blessing: </b>The Lodge member starts with Perfect Impression on every Social Maneuvering with those with the Homeless or Outsider conditions. When spending Willpower to add dices on Streetwise roll, he gains the rote quality on that roll.<br /> <b>Aspiration:</b> To gather information on local city.<br /> <b>Ban:</b> A Lodge member cannot refuse to provide aid to the impoverished.<br /> <br /> The Lodge Sacred Hunt grants your character the ability to track prey by word of mouth, adding their contacts dots to tracking rolls as an equipment bonus.<br /> <br /> Many of Bone Gnawers Lodge members have these Conditions:<br /> <br /> <b>Homeless (Persistent)</b><br /> The character doesn't have a home of his own and probably lives on the street. The character needs to succeed on a Survival or Streetwise roll to find suitable shelter for a night's rest. Failure to do so likely exposes him to the effects of fatigue, or other environmental tilts. Forced starvation or dehydration can lead her to Deprived Condition or even Sick Tilt. Characters who clearly display their homelessness have -1 to social rolls without the condition.<br /> <b>Possible Sources:</b> Tragedy. Lost of wealth or job.<br /> <b>Resolution:</b> Getting steady income enough to sustain living in normal accommodation for at least month (attaining a resources rating). Help from close ones, letting to support character.<br /> <b>Beat:</b> Character is refused basic aid or human dignity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Did a few corrections, most notably the ban, how the blessing works and the benefit of the Sacred Hunt rite.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":576,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","user":"Ephsy","date":". 04-21-2016, 05:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-21T17:59:57-07:00","id":870803,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar576_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"576\" data-vbnamecard=\"576\">Ephsy</a> , thanks for changing on wording, in general Bone Gnawers description. But as to mechanics - I'm not so sure. I will need to think on them for few days. Nonetheless, thank your for corrections.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-21T20:18:21-07:00","id":870874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/867500-apocalypse-tribes-as-2e-lodges?p=870803#post870803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar576_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"576\" data-vbnamecard=\"576\">Ephsy</a> , thanks for changing on wording, in general Bone Gnawers description. But as to mechanics - I'm not so sure. I will need to think on them for few days. Nonetheless, thank your for corrections.</div> </div> </div> </div>The reason for the changes? Urban settings use Streetwise for tracking, the previous ban basically made you any homeless person their bitch, and the sacred hunt perk was a straight up copy from Thousand Steel Teeth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-21T20:19:09-07:00","id":870876,"title":"","content":"And my idea on <i>Silver Fangs</i>. Still, do not have good concepts on their Bonds to written with.<br /> <br /> <b>Silver Fangs</b><br /> <i>Nobles, </i><i>Houses of Sun and Moon</i><i>, B</i><i>oyar</i><i>s</i><br /> \u201cNoblesse oblige.\u201d Being noble is obligation - to country, to people - and first and foremost - to family. It\u2019s most crucial thing to <i>Silver Fangs</i>, Lodge dedicated to \u2018proper\u2019 ruling of Uratha - by them and their kin. Heirs to great heroes and leaders, they pass they greatness till this day.<br /> <br /> They come from terrains of now Russia - but in that time they were all varying tribes, fighting with each other. Under guidance of Falcon, one group finally take control and initiated all chieftains and rulers to come to cult of their patron. Under their secret Totem, <i>Silver Fangs </i>remade human tribes in to kingdoms, and those in to empires. They spread all over the world, always making sure \u201ctheir own\u201d are real force in power. There were only one problem - ancestors.<br /> <br /> Original <i>Fangs </i>were coming from the lines started even in Pangea. Descendants of what would be once Ivory Claws Tribe under Silver Wolf, were meticulous to point to their great forefathers. But then came great schism - Lodge was divided on the matter of joining new heroes as noble ancestors. One side say only original predecessors were worthy of veneration and no new line could join their fold. Other group said there is place for new idols and their own posterity in Lodge. Two sides split, one joining Ivory Claws and making sure no new blood will pollute their kin. Second seek guidance under Winter Wolf in not showing weakness of shortsightness their once brothers shown. They become so called Houses of Sun and Moon - first for close relations with Helios and hatred for Forsaken \u201cmongrels\u201d. Second for joining Luna and her Tribes of Moon, especially Storm Lords. Rest is, like they say, just history.<br /> <br /> <b>Totem:</b> Falcon<br /> Falcon is both most dedicated and one of most vain of avian spirits. It\u2019s royal majesty is awestrucking, but also making you easy target for his hunt on you. His both literal and social predator, taking what he needs, when he needs.<br /> As Totem, Falcon actively support both Houses and their Tribes in Lodge. Pure and Forsaken war is not his concern, at least till his children do what he says. In his eyes, conflict of two groups is even <i>better</i> - pushed to the limits for other side, Silver Fangs are perfecting themselves in their role as leaders. Regardless before which Firstborn they answer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 04-22-2016, 02:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T09:33:55-08:00","id":1010228,"title":"","content":"Got idea for the most disliked old Tribe that I hope will make interesting Lodge now. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <b>Children of Gaia</b><br /> <i>Children of Unicorn, </i><i>Harmonious, Purists</i><br /> Gaia is all around us. In streams and rivers, in mountains and trees. In animals and humans. And especially in Shadow. To be true, Earth\u2019s Shadow <i>is </i>Gaia. And just like Uratha are part of Shadow, they are part of Gaia. We are part of Gaia. Gaia is part of us. We are part of Harmony.<br /> <br /> But there are places that should not be. Places twisted and corrupted. They are those that turn around from our purpose. Those that lost their way and gone astray. And those that turn from Gaia, need to be dealt with. We should save our brothers and sisters, if we can. Restore them to true way. And lead them to final resting place, if we cannot.<br /> <br /> Children of Gaia seek to help Uratha in maintaining Harmony. They seek to improve those that goes too much in ways of Flesh or Spirit. To clean the material and Hisil worlds, return them to balance. They clean Wounds and heal Uratha hearts. And they truly despise Bale Hounds and their treacheries.<br /> <br /> Lodge is open to member from all Tribes of Moon, but Blood Talons rarely join it, seeing them as to \u2018soft\u2019. Hunters in Darkness are probably the most numerous in pursuit of Purity, but Bone Shadows trying to understand relations of Harmony to Shadow are second after them. More farseeing Storm Lords enter Lodge to show rest of Uratha better way to their victories.<br /> <br /> <b>Totem:</b> Unicorn<br /> Unicorn if one of purest of spirits, compassionate in peace but also ferocious in war. He leads his children to make Shadow clean of unnatural tendencies and be true to themselves and ways of their People. Finally, to strike those that spoil it for all around.<br /> <br /> <b>Bonds</b><br /> <b>Blessing: </b>The Lodge member can easier maintain his Harmony. He get\u2019s constant +1 bonus on any Breaking Point roll, irrelevant if to Flesh or to Spirit.<br /> <b>Aspiration:</b> To purify Shadow and Material Realm.<br /> <b>Ban:</b> A Lodge member must destroy any corruption of Shadow.<br /> <br /> <b>The Sacred Hunt</b><br /> The Lodge Sacred Hunt grants your character the ability to sense corruption in things. He gets supernatural sense on Wounds related phenomena, even when they are disguised. He also can feel unbalanced werewolves \u2013 those of Harmony 10-9 and 1-2.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-01T01:26:04-08:00","id":1010552,"title":"","content":"Here is the Tribe that need to change most as the Lodge \u2013 With Iron Masters being almost entirely what Glass Walkers being in Apocalypse, I needed to fine new focus for them as Cult of Hunt. As \u2018Adaptability\u2019 and \u2018Survival\u2019 is impossible to hunt for and Red Wolf took much of this ideas in to herself as Firstborn \u2013 I made controversial decision and changed Totem of them from Cockroach to Ant, leading them to be more builders and modernists, that solely survivors what they would be following original Totem. I hope you like it, even with changes so great there. I think that characters of Max Roman from official Colorado setting would be perfect for this Lodge.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Glass Walkers</b></span><br /> <i>Workers, </i><i>Protectors, ???</i><br /> <br /> Glass is one of humanities first true creations \u2013 art in the pure form. There were earlier accomplishments and inventions, but glass was first thing done only as ornate, only to please eye. Glass is very delicate. Like relationships between us.<br /> <br /> By legends, glass making was discovered by humanity in ancient Mesopotamia. Same region that hosted Sumerican City of Bau - a place where man, spirit and werewolf live together in awareness of one another, with man appeasing spirit and worshipping the Dog-Kings of Sumer\u2014the Ur-Sag, the dog-headed heroes. Where lone werewolf sects become Tribes of Moon. Where they created first ever created Protectorate. ( See <b>Forsaken Chrocniler\u2019s Guide III \u2013 To Transform </b>)<br /> <br /> Then called Glass Workers, they were there when City of Bau rose. They seeded true Uratha society, based on herds models and changing times. They reminded their brothers and sisters that Pangea felt centuries before and it\u2019s time to move forward. It\u2019s time to adapt and build new werewolf society. Better society.<br /> <br /> Like glass is shaped, all the traditions and norms are shaped by the people making them. Glass Workers made rest of werewolves to become Tribes we know them today and spark the new Protectorates \u2013 like the City of Bau \u2013 where they can. \u2018Uratha are one People\u2019, and like humans, they need community. So Lodge will form it for them, just like humans were making beautiful glass art for centuries. But as City of Bau have fallen, all Protectorates come to their end. Just like human societies, sooner or later old Uratha communities fall apart and need to be reworked. It\u2019s okay, Lodge is there to end it and start the seed of new structure.<br /> <br /> From XX century era of skyscrapers they love to live in \u2013 as most Protectorates come to being in cities - Lodge renamed to Glass Walkers are guardians and makers of them around the world. They understand that each werewolf community is different, but they try each time to seed new society and cooperation. They also point out the moments were old system stops to work and it\u2019s time to remake it into something new, just like glass need to be shaped into new form when it\u2019s lose it\u2019s purpose. They hunt traitors, interlopers or just threats to local Protectorates. They look for cubs to join next packs of existing communities and look for new dangers they can brought. And all the time they look for ways to improve Protectorates, based on human society inventions.<br /> <br /> Glass Walkers are entwined with Tribes of Moon. As City of Bau were first Protectorate, so them cultivate it\u2019s traditions of change. Most of members are from Iron Masters, as they focus on shifting societies and how Uratha can take what\u2019s best of human organizations. Rest are generally Storm Lords, concerned with how to lead Uratha and what changes to local laws need to be brought for community of People can thrive.<br /> <br /> <b>Totem:</b> Ant<br /> Glass Walkers follow tireless Ant, that build and rebuild. Like her physical children, when structure is weakening, they need to repair it. Finally, structures cannot be remade, and new \u2018hive\u2019 need to be started.<br /> <br /> <b>Bonds</b><br /> <b>Blessing: </b>Adherent have one level better Impression with his own Protectorate members and 9-Again ability on any roll for Opening Doors.<br /> <b>Aspiration:</b> To build and defend Protectorate.<br /> <b>Ban:</b> A Lodge member cannot live more than lunar month outside of Protectorate territory.<br /> <br /> <b>The Sacred Hunt</b><br /> The Lodge Sacred Hunt grants your character the ability to track weakness to the Protectorate \u2013 sensing \u2018weak spots\u2019, pointing to future problems for society. He will have sensation that some Uratha or spirit is trying to betray community, trying to break it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-01T04:22:45-08:00","id":1010576,"title":"","content":"And next Tribe to join family of Lodges. I hope that this Fianna works closely with Apocalypse original. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Fianna</b></span><br /> <i>Children of Stag, </i><i>Bards, Tale-Seekers</i><br /> \u201cWe will remember.\u201d Its the motto for the Uratha children of Stag. Hailing from celtic oral tradition, this Lodge is dedicated to uncovering stories and songs because they are making People what they are now. Fianna are especially dedicated to finding tales from times of Pangea and hunts of Urfarah. They say they will let them better understand how world should work, even after Sundering.<br /> <br /> In their search of stories, Lodge has more than once crossed they claws with weird, faerie beings that are best understood as Living Stories. As experts on tales and howls, they took on to themselves to solve those problems. When no fighting with this Fae invasions on local territory, Fianna are said to exchange treaties, oaths and even love relationships with lesser of this otherworldly kind. Still, they first and formost role is to collect lore and tales of Uratha, to used them here and now.<br /> <br /> Tribes in Lodge are dominated by Bone Shadows that always look for new lore and Iron Masters that thinks in stories are hints to new ways. Interestingly, high is number of Hunters in Darkness, that wants return of \u2018old ways\u2019 and remembering deeds of Urfarfah and ancestors.<br /> <br /> <b>Totem:</b> Stag <br /> Fianna follow Stag, spirit made from the love of life itself. Their patron teach them to catch every moment, but also remember deeds of those that passed away. Both should cherish the most glorious moments.<br /> <br /> As Stag is spirit of non-predator, many Uratha thinks that Fianna do not have \u2018guts\u2019 to truly fight, only spending times searching for next tale or love interest. Reality is that Bards can be very drive to find their answers, even with tearing others with their claws. In the end, Stag still has antlers that he can stab you with.<br /> <br /> <b>Bonds</b><br /> <b>Blessing: </b>One per night, Fianna can rise his packs spirit with inspiring tale, like the Inspiring Merit.<br /> <b>Aspiration:</b> To gather lore about werewolves in local population.<br /> <b>Ban:</b> A Lodge member cannot leave occasion too hear new tale.<br /> <br /> <b>The Sacred Hunt</b><br /> The Lodge Sacred Hunt grants your character the ability to use up to his Primal Urge times of Inspired Condition in Siskur-Dah on any roll connected to Prey.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}